1
00:00:06,193 --> 00:00:08,612
5 CONTESTANTS LEFT.
3 DAYS AND 1 HOUR UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.

2
00:00:19,748 --> 00:00:21,083
Don't move!

3
00:00:23,293 --> 00:00:26,421
Is this guy's life worth a lot?

4
00:00:29,925 --> 00:00:31,301
What's wrong?

5
00:00:32,594 --> 00:00:34,513
Someone's watching us.

6
00:00:36,056 --> 00:00:37,603
Not the police.

7
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,563
Why him...?

8
00:00:56,535 --> 00:00:57,452
Yes?

9
00:00:57,786 --> 00:01:03,500
Mr. Niide, this is Andy Won's
secretary speaking. My name is Chan.

10
00:01:04,543 --> 00:01:07,546
There's a matter I'd like
to bring to your attention.

11
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:09,840
To my attention?

12
00:01:11,717 --> 00:01:17,180
I ask that you not take your eyes off Andy.

13
00:01:17,597 --> 00:01:20,142
He holds the whole truth.

14
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:25,313
He knows who's behind all this? Who?

15
00:01:26,064 --> 00:01:28,442
I do not know. But he does.

16
00:01:29,818 --> 00:01:31,445
Why are you telling me this?

17
00:01:31,862 --> 00:01:36,616
Because you said you would free
all the hostages. I feel the same way.

18
00:01:36,742 --> 00:01:39,661
Please save Sylvia.

19
00:01:40,537 --> 00:01:42,747
I cannot contact you any further.

20
00:01:42,873 --> 00:01:45,250
We'll be waiting for you in Hong Kong.

21
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:46,710
Yeah, but...

22
00:02:02,851 --> 00:02:04,686
PM 05:08 JST
TOKYO HANEDA AIRPORT

23
00:02:04,811 --> 00:02:06,021
It's time, sir.

24
00:02:06,813 --> 00:02:08,440
And the guy in Hong Kong?

25
00:02:09,107 --> 00:02:10,901
He's still keeping silent.

26
00:02:19,534 --> 00:02:20,577
Good.

27
00:02:27,918 --> 00:02:30,712
Thoughts on the secretary's call?

28
00:02:31,296 --> 00:02:35,008
Andy's definitely hiding something.

29
00:02:40,764 --> 00:02:42,516
JANICE LAU

30
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,566
Hello?

31
00:02:51,691 --> 00:02:56,154
Kiju, right? I'm Janice, Janice Lau.

32
00:02:56,571 --> 00:02:59,866
Ah, Singapore. What's the matter?

33
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:01,660
Are you alone?

34
00:03:03,912 --> 00:03:06,164
Yes, I'm alone.

35
00:03:06,831 --> 00:03:12,170
So I've been thinking, and...

36
00:03:13,421 --> 00:03:15,632
I still don't trust that cop you're with.

37
00:03:16,675 --> 00:03:21,096
You don't trust Niide...
because he voted for you?

38
00:03:21,221 --> 00:03:25,559
He tried to kick me off the game,
can you believe it?

39
00:03:26,476 --> 00:03:28,186
I trusted him!

40
00:03:29,437 --> 00:03:34,526
He's going to double-cross us
one by one to save his wife. I know it.

41
00:03:37,112 --> 00:03:39,322
What am I supposed to do about it?

42
00:03:41,449 --> 00:03:42,909
Work with me.

43
00:03:44,077 --> 00:03:45,328
Why should I work with you?

44
00:03:48,248 --> 00:03:50,458
I realized who the kidnapper is.

45
00:03:54,504 --> 00:03:55,797
Who's the kidnapper?

46
00:03:56,214 --> 00:03:58,258
You think I can just tell you?

47
00:03:59,718 --> 00:04:04,055
If you want to know,
come to Singapore and help me.

48
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:07,434
Fine. But I need some kind of proof.

49
00:04:10,979 --> 00:04:12,898
You don't have to believe me...

50
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:17,235
I thought I could trust you,
but I'll find someone else.

51
00:04:31,458 --> 00:04:36,004
CHECKPOINT 4: GO AROUND THE CLOCK
THE TIME LIMIT IS 30 HOURS

52
00:04:39,591 --> 00:04:44,012
She said she knows who the kidnapper is.
Wants to cooperate.

53
00:04:45,805 --> 00:04:47,849
She's probably lying.

54
00:04:47,974 --> 00:04:52,729
Yeah. She might not be, though.

55
00:04:54,606 --> 00:04:57,400
I don't know what's true and what's not.

56
00:04:58,985 --> 00:05:01,071
Who's an ally and who's a foe.

57
00:05:02,238 --> 00:05:07,994
Trust me. I'll trust you, and only you.

58
00:05:12,499 --> 00:05:14,292
We should split up.

59
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:18,421
Rendezvous with Janice in Singapore.

60
00:05:19,255 --> 00:05:22,509
I'll go to Hong Kong.

61
00:05:24,719 --> 00:05:28,848
-I also use Uchiake.
-Thank you.

62
00:05:29,015 --> 00:05:32,227
Users can share their worries with an AI

63
00:05:32,352 --> 00:05:35,230
that provides empathetic responses.

64
00:05:35,397 --> 00:05:36,773
What inspired you?

65
00:05:37,232 --> 00:05:42,904
I never met my parents.
I'm all alone in the world.

66
00:05:43,697 --> 00:05:45,198
As a child,

67
00:05:45,323 --> 00:05:48,910
I wanted to share
that hidden pain with someone.

68
00:05:50,328 --> 00:05:53,206
That's why I made Uchiake.

69
00:05:53,331 --> 00:05:57,419
-Is that Higa?
-Yeah. It's an interview from way back.

70
00:05:58,670 --> 00:06:01,589
Uchiake. It made waves in Korea, too.

71
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:07,971
And everywhere else. People were hailing Higa
as some kind of global innovator.

72
00:06:08,471 --> 00:06:10,974
Should I really go to Singapore?

73
00:06:12,976 --> 00:06:16,730
Something good
is sure to happen in Singapore.

74
00:06:18,314 --> 00:06:21,985
It only ever agrees with the user.

75
00:06:23,236 --> 00:06:27,407
No doubt people prefer that
to harsh realities.

76
00:06:30,618 --> 00:06:35,039
You know, I wonder why Higa said
he was always alone.

77
00:06:36,624 --> 00:06:39,544
His sin was vanity.

78
00:06:40,086 --> 00:06:43,089
He built his career on lies, remember?

79
00:06:45,133 --> 00:06:50,805
His sick mother was kidnapped.
We know that at least.

80
00:06:57,103 --> 00:07:01,232
PM 05:49 JST
NAHA

81
00:07:24,172 --> 00:07:27,092
How much more will you make me suffer?

82
00:07:27,217 --> 00:07:29,469
How are you suffering?

83
00:07:29,594 --> 00:07:31,930
Don't torment me anymore.

84
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:39,104
Just die, I beg you...

85
00:07:43,066 --> 00:07:44,317
Mother.

86
00:08:41,833 --> 00:08:43,251
What do you want?

87
00:08:43,376 --> 00:08:46,462
It's Niide.
I need to ask you something.

88
00:08:47,422 --> 00:08:49,465
I have nothing to say to you.

89
00:08:49,757 --> 00:08:51,676
Five years ago...

90
00:08:51,926 --> 00:08:54,929
What happened to you five years ago?

91
00:08:57,974 --> 00:08:59,142
"Mission.

92
00:08:59,934 --> 00:09:03,855
"Release proof
that you falsified water quality data

93
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:09,652
"for the thermal power plant
construction project five years ago."

94
00:09:12,488 --> 00:09:16,034
You said you weren't in Tokyo five years ago.

95
00:09:16,159 --> 00:09:17,785
What were you doing?

96
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:23,082
You struck it rich again five years ago.
What happened?

97
00:09:23,207 --> 00:09:26,753
Shut up about five years ago!
Hell if I know!

98
00:09:26,878 --> 00:09:30,006
I need clues on the Mastermind.
Help me out.

99
00:09:30,131 --> 00:09:34,177
I'm trying to rescue everyone,
including your mother!

100
00:09:39,599 --> 00:09:41,726
I will complete my mission.

101
00:09:42,727 --> 00:09:46,689
Not to save my mother...

102
00:09:47,523 --> 00:09:51,861
But to beat this stupid game.
To be the winner!

103
00:10:12,173 --> 00:10:13,883
UCHIAKE

104
00:10:14,759 --> 00:10:20,936
I'm like this because of you.
It's all your fault, Mother.

105
00:10:26,854 --> 00:10:29,107
Why was our family different?

106
00:10:30,233 --> 00:10:33,069
Why were you different from other mothers?

107
00:10:37,657 --> 00:10:40,163
Higa, isn't that your mom?

108
00:10:40,223 --> 00:10:46,416
-She's working at a construction site.
-Your family's so poor.

109
00:10:46,514 --> 00:10:48,808
I was always miserable...

110
00:10:50,249 --> 00:10:51,751
Especially that day...

111
00:10:54,382 --> 00:10:56,718
Kuranosuke! What happened?!

112
00:10:58,052 --> 00:11:00,013
Higa tried to steal this.

113
00:11:00,763 --> 00:11:03,391
No! I wasn't stealing it!

114
00:11:03,599 --> 00:11:07,103
Thief!
Why not get your mom to buy you one?

115
00:11:07,603 --> 00:11:09,605
Yuta, that's enough.

116
00:11:12,608 --> 00:11:14,444
We have a problem.

117
00:11:15,611 --> 00:11:17,572
Please forgive us!

118
00:11:21,909 --> 00:11:26,622
No... I... I'm not a thief...

119
00:11:28,750 --> 00:11:31,210
That day, I made up my mind.

120
00:11:39,177 --> 00:11:41,929
I swore not to live a life like yours.

121
00:11:42,221 --> 00:11:44,515
I'd never be a loser like you.

122
00:11:46,350 --> 00:11:52,523
After that, I studied
and worked like crazy to win.

123
00:11:53,524 --> 00:11:56,903
I drove away the clinging stink of poverty.

124
00:11:58,404 --> 00:12:03,326
I was reborn. A whole new life was mine...

125
00:12:04,285 --> 00:12:09,665
I never met my parents.
I'm all alone in the world.

126
00:12:10,666 --> 00:12:12,168
As a child,

127
00:12:12,293 --> 00:12:15,963
I wanted to share
that hidden pain with someone.

128
00:12:17,006 --> 00:12:18,549
I had won...

129
00:12:22,178 --> 00:12:26,474
AM 00:30 JST

130
00:12:29,185 --> 00:12:36,400
But I couldn't shake the misfortune
and misery you gave me.

131
00:12:36,685 --> 00:12:39,562
You know what this is?

132
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:43,233
-No, what is it?
-Uchiake. Don't you know?

133
00:12:43,775 --> 00:12:46,486
-So retro!
-Hey.

134
00:12:46,867 --> 00:12:50,482
CEO Kuranosuke Higa here developed it.

135
00:12:50,507 --> 00:12:53,134
Wow, you're so young for a CEO!

136
00:12:53,172 --> 00:12:56,342
He's a global innovator,
the pride of Okinawa.

137
00:12:56,454 --> 00:12:59,207
Really? Wow!

138
00:12:59,332 --> 00:13:01,793
That was a long time ago, though.

139
00:13:03,044 --> 00:13:06,548
-How rude!
-I'm just kidding.

140
00:13:07,674 --> 00:13:09,759
I heard money's tight.

141
00:13:10,885 --> 00:13:14,973
I need funds, or it's not gonna end well.

142
00:13:16,516 --> 00:13:21,771
You know about the thermal power plant
my company's trying to build?

143
00:13:23,606 --> 00:13:26,192
-In Yanbaru?
-Yeah.

144
00:13:26,943 --> 00:13:29,946
We hit a snag with water quality results.

145
00:13:30,366 --> 00:13:32,129
Throws a wrench in the works.

146
00:13:33,410 --> 00:13:34,576
What would you do?

147
00:13:36,859 --> 00:13:39,043
You want me to... overwrite the data?

148
00:13:42,083 --> 00:13:46,296
The only way
to escape my accursed life and succeed

149
00:13:46,421 --> 00:13:48,798
was to sell my soul.

150
00:13:49,758 --> 00:13:52,510
After that, it was a downward spiral.

151
00:13:53,678 --> 00:13:59,309
All just to win. I wanted to keep winning.

152
00:14:02,437 --> 00:14:07,233
I've got another job
for my trusted business partner.

153
00:14:07,525 --> 00:14:08,693
Sure...

154
00:14:10,695 --> 00:14:12,364
I'm in.

155
00:14:17,077 --> 00:14:21,414
I succeeded and bought you
your own home, didn't I?

156
00:14:21,998 --> 00:14:26,669
Why couldn't you be happy about it?

157
00:14:27,295 --> 00:14:31,883
Would it be okay
if I invite some old friends over?

158
00:14:32,050 --> 00:14:34,594
Like former co-workers and neighbors.

159
00:14:34,761 --> 00:14:38,723
You think they'll like that?
They'll only resent you.

160
00:14:39,474 --> 00:14:40,475
I miss them.

161
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:43,978
You're here now! In my world!

162
00:14:44,521 --> 00:14:47,899
Don't you get it?
Your son is a world-famous CEO!

163
00:15:01,788 --> 00:15:08,837
Mother, I failed to break your curse
of poverty and misery, didn't I?

164
00:15:11,756 --> 00:15:13,758
That's why this happened.

165
00:15:15,969 --> 00:15:18,012
Kuranosuke, I waited for you.

166
00:15:18,638 --> 00:15:23,893
It's just about ready,
so go wash your hands...

167
00:15:25,478 --> 00:15:27,564
Who are you?! Who...?!

168
00:15:39,576 --> 00:15:41,369
TOMIKO

169
00:15:41,494 --> 00:15:44,664
YOU HAVE BEEN ENLISTED IN THE KIDNAP GAME

170
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:50,628
My mission is to confess to a crime
I committed five years ago.

171
00:15:51,129 --> 00:15:55,800
If I do that, I'll be seen as a criminal.

172
00:15:58,928 --> 00:16:03,141
Everything I've done will be unearthed,
one by one.

173
00:16:05,351 --> 00:16:08,021
I'll lose everything!

174
00:16:09,606 --> 00:16:13,026
That's sad. Such a shame.

175
00:16:15,570 --> 00:16:20,903
Even so, I can't afford to lose this game.

176
00:16:21,576 --> 00:16:24,996
That's right. You need to keep on winning.

177
00:16:26,164 --> 00:16:29,125
To prove that I overwrote the data,

178
00:16:29,417 --> 00:16:34,923
I need to steal the log from the server room
at the prefectural office.

179
00:16:39,135 --> 00:16:41,638
So far it's going well.

180
00:16:52,482 --> 00:16:54,400
REQUESTING VIRUS CHECK

181
00:16:54,525 --> 00:16:56,778
OKINAWA SANITATION DEPARTMENT

182
00:16:58,446 --> 00:16:59,656
Bingo!

183
00:17:01,074 --> 00:17:03,785
SINGAPORE
AM 06:51 SGT

184
00:17:04,577 --> 00:17:09,666
Go around the clock...
What does this even mean?

185
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,879
Meanwhile, due to the impact
of the Arctic polar vortex,

186
00:17:15,004 --> 00:17:18,341
temperatures in the Northern Hemisphere
are expected to drop.

187
00:17:18,466 --> 00:17:24,639
Some regions may also experience rough weather
accompanied by heavy snowfall or strong winds.

188
00:17:26,349 --> 00:17:28,351
Where is there a vortex...?

189
00:17:33,648 --> 00:17:36,609
I'm in Singapore now. At the airport.

190
00:17:37,026 --> 00:17:40,113
What? I thought you didn't trust me.

191
00:17:40,238 --> 00:17:43,533
Your mission's like a chain of riddles, isn't it?

192
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:48,454
In which case, I can at least help you
keep your boyfriend alive.

193
00:17:48,579 --> 00:17:50,957
I can't tell you
who the kidnapper is for nothing.

194
00:17:51,374 --> 00:17:56,921
I know. Anyway, where are you?

195
00:17:57,046 --> 00:17:59,882
On the way to the airport.
It's my fourth checkpoint.

196
00:18:00,008 --> 00:18:04,012
The clue was a blue vortex and the words,
"Go Around The Clock."

197
00:18:04,137 --> 00:18:07,765
So where is there a vortex?
It must be the Jewel Rain Vortex!

198
00:18:07,890 --> 00:18:10,226
That's where I'm going.
Wait for me there, okay?

199
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:12,103
All right.

200
00:18:22,697 --> 00:18:25,742
HONG KONG

201
00:18:38,755 --> 00:18:40,465
The other people...

202
00:18:43,176 --> 00:18:45,511
Are the other hostages safe?

203
00:18:55,605 --> 00:19:00,318
What about the child?
There was a little girl.

204
00:19:01,486 --> 00:19:07,825
Please, help them.
You only need one hostage, right?

205
00:19:09,911 --> 00:19:11,454
Let it be me.

206
00:19:11,788 --> 00:19:14,707
Saori... What are you saying? No!

207
00:19:21,089 --> 00:19:23,007
CANNOT OPEN PAGE

208
00:19:31,099 --> 00:19:33,434
NAHA

209
00:19:35,463 --> 00:19:38,174
Get into the server room,

210
00:19:38,299 --> 00:19:41,594
steal the transaction log, and publish it.

211
00:19:42,178 --> 00:19:44,097
Then I win.

212
00:20:11,070 --> 00:20:12,822
What? I'm almost there!

213
00:20:12,947 --> 00:20:14,198
Tell me the clue again.

214
00:20:15,575 --> 00:20:16,450
What?

215
00:20:17,201 --> 00:20:19,453
This might not be the place!

216
00:20:19,662 --> 00:20:20,621
What do you mean?!

217
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:22,373
Just tell me the clue!

218
00:20:24,208 --> 00:20:28,921
A blue vortex with the words,
"Go Around The Clock."

219
00:20:29,881 --> 00:20:31,632
Wait. I'll send it to you.

220
00:20:37,138 --> 00:20:41,267
I knew it. This is the wrong place.

221
00:20:41,976 --> 00:20:43,269
How is it wrong?!

222
00:20:43,686 --> 00:20:49,609
A vortex is dynamic.
So, we need to look for a static structure...

223
00:20:49,734 --> 00:20:52,361
More like a helix.

224
00:20:52,862 --> 00:20:54,155
A helix?

225
00:20:54,739 --> 00:21:00,870
I'm sure you're familiar
with the Helix Bridge. Right?

226
00:21:01,579 --> 00:21:05,958
Helix Bridge? Yeah, I know.

227
00:21:06,083 --> 00:21:11,881
It's modeled on a strand of DNA,
but it twists to the left.

228
00:21:12,215 --> 00:21:17,220
There are letters on the deck
symbolizing nucleotides.

229
00:21:17,595 --> 00:21:19,347
G, A, T, C.

230
00:21:20,014 --> 00:21:22,058
So what?! I don't understand!

231
00:21:22,266 --> 00:21:27,438
"Go Around The Clock."
The first letters match!

232
00:21:30,066 --> 00:21:31,108
That means...

233
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:34,987
It's not the Rain Vortex, it's the...

234
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:37,865
Helix Bridge.

235
00:21:41,118 --> 00:21:44,163
Stop! Take me to the Helix Bridge!

236
00:21:52,213 --> 00:21:56,884
AM 07:18 HKT
HONG KONG

237
00:21:58,886 --> 00:21:59,929
Hello.

238
00:22:00,429 --> 00:22:02,056
I'd like to talk to Andy.

239
00:22:02,181 --> 00:22:04,266
Tell him Toshiro Niide is here.

240
00:22:04,558 --> 00:22:07,478
I'm sorry,
Mister Wong is not in the office today.

241
00:22:09,313 --> 00:22:12,233
I'm here about the kiDnap GAME.

242
00:22:14,443 --> 00:22:16,612
Andy's sister's life is in danger.

243
00:22:16,737 --> 00:22:20,491
Now isn't the time to be evasive.

244
00:22:20,741 --> 00:22:22,660
I really don't know where he is.

245
00:22:22,785 --> 00:22:25,871
He's been out since the day before yesterday.

246
00:22:28,749 --> 00:22:32,253
What about his secretary, Mr. Chan?

247
00:22:32,378 --> 00:22:36,215
I believe he left together with Andy,
but I'm afraid I don't know any further.

248
00:22:42,013 --> 00:22:44,306
Sorry. Thanks.

249
00:23:31,569 --> 00:23:34,447
QUICK SCAN
SWEET FRUIT VIRUS FOUND

250
00:23:34,565 --> 00:23:38,694
Seems to be a new kind of virus.
It's a cyberattack.

251
00:23:38,819 --> 00:23:41,238
Our security should be airtight.

252
00:23:41,363 --> 00:23:44,992
Cyberattacks grow
more sophisticated every year.

253
00:23:45,117 --> 00:23:48,537
It causes noisy audio and network latency.

254
00:23:48,662 --> 00:23:52,625
-Sound familiar?
-Yes, exactly that!

255
00:23:52,750 --> 00:23:56,211
There's a risk to citizens' personal data

256
00:23:56,337 --> 00:23:58,672
and other private information.

257
00:24:00,215 --> 00:24:02,343
What do we do, Mr. Yamanaka?

258
00:24:02,468 --> 00:24:07,014
Leave it to me.
I'll run a scan of the server directly.

259
00:24:07,139 --> 00:24:08,432
Thank you.

260
00:24:15,397 --> 00:24:16,482
This way.

261
00:24:23,238 --> 00:24:24,865
This is the server.

262
00:24:25,699 --> 00:24:28,744
-I'll connect my laptop to scan it.
-Sure.

263
00:24:37,419 --> 00:24:40,839
It'll take time.
I'll call you when I'm done.

264
00:24:40,964 --> 00:24:42,299
Understood.

265
00:25:27,474 --> 00:25:28,683
This is it.

266
00:26:08,755 --> 00:26:11,681
"Go Around The Clock"...

267
00:26:12,188 --> 00:26:15,321
Clockwise...

268
00:26:18,683 --> 00:26:20,268
It's the other side!

269
00:26:27,939 --> 00:26:31,234
-I'm impressed.
-Nah, it's no big deal.

270
00:26:32,315 --> 00:26:34,526
-Keep at it.
-I will.

271
00:26:36,391 --> 00:26:40,636
Thief!
Why not get your mom to buy you one?

272
00:26:41,832 --> 00:26:44,543
-You'll reach that level soon.
-Yeah?

273
00:26:44,668 --> 00:26:47,671
-I'll do my best.
-We're both doing fine.

274
00:26:50,966 --> 00:26:52,259
Higa?

275
00:27:04,187 --> 00:27:06,064
Hey! Watch it!

276
00:27:42,434 --> 00:27:43,643
That you, Higa?

277
00:27:45,228 --> 00:27:48,148
It is you! Do you remember me?

278
00:27:48,398 --> 00:27:52,360
Kanna, Yuta Kanna!
We went to school together!

279
00:27:53,945 --> 00:27:56,698
Yeah... I remember.

280
00:27:57,657 --> 00:27:59,242
You're in a tight spot.

281
00:27:59,367 --> 00:28:02,329
The kiDnap GAME.
I heard about your mom.

282
00:28:04,414 --> 00:28:07,209
Mother's been found. She's safe.

283
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:09,377
Really? That's great.

284
00:28:10,212 --> 00:28:11,630
I'm in a hurry.

285
00:28:14,382 --> 00:28:20,639
Your mom must be glad to see
the fine man you grew up to be.

286
00:28:21,306 --> 00:28:23,600
It's like she said back then.

287
00:28:24,851 --> 00:28:26,811
Please forgive me!

288
00:28:31,149 --> 00:28:35,862
No... I... I'm not a thief...

289
00:28:46,373 --> 00:28:48,500
You shouldn't apologize.

290
00:28:48,625 --> 00:28:51,670
You should discipline him.

291
00:28:54,506 --> 00:28:57,092
Kuranosuke didn't steal it.

292
00:28:58,843 --> 00:29:02,806
This misunderstanding happened
because of my poverty.

293
00:29:02,931 --> 00:29:05,183
That's why I'm apologizing.

294
00:29:06,059 --> 00:29:10,355
Kuranosuke will become a fine man.
In spite of my failure.

295
00:29:10,897 --> 00:29:13,775
He'll bring happiness to everyone.

296
00:29:14,734 --> 00:29:16,069
Why...?

297
00:29:19,364 --> 00:29:21,825
Why do you tell me that now?

298
00:29:22,951 --> 00:29:24,411
What's wrong?

299
00:29:26,162 --> 00:29:28,081
Me, a fine man?

300
00:29:30,709 --> 00:29:33,295
Me, bring happiness to everyone?

301
00:29:34,713 --> 00:29:36,214
Mr. Yamanaka!

302
00:29:38,216 --> 00:29:43,597
I've been looking for you everywhere!
Have you finished?

303
00:29:47,142 --> 00:29:49,561
-Mr. Yamanaka?
-Who's Mr. Yamanaka?

304
00:29:53,898 --> 00:29:55,025
Higa?!

305
00:29:55,150 --> 00:29:57,027
Stop him!

306
00:30:08,413 --> 00:30:13,043
Look at me, Mother.
Look what I've become.

307
00:30:18,715 --> 00:30:20,592
How could you love...

308
00:30:32,395 --> 00:30:35,148
a son like me so much?

309
00:31:27,951 --> 00:31:29,411
This blasted game!

310
00:31:44,676 --> 00:31:46,469
kiDnap GAME...

311
00:32:01,609 --> 00:32:03,069
You're finished.

312
00:32:03,194 --> 00:32:06,489
UCHIAKE CEO
FALSIFIED WATER QUALITY DATA

313
00:32:23,298 --> 00:32:25,800
NO INTERNET CONNECTION

314
00:32:34,517 --> 00:32:35,643
Why...?

315
00:32:38,229 --> 00:32:40,732
I can't let you complete your mission.

316
00:32:48,031 --> 00:32:49,324
You...

317
00:33:00,376 --> 00:33:02,921
Is this your doing?

318
00:33:03,421 --> 00:33:06,257
It's the same as what you did.

319
00:33:08,635 --> 00:33:10,011
Why?

320
00:33:11,012 --> 00:33:12,931
Made it...

321
00:33:16,267 --> 00:33:19,646
If you give me that laptop, I won't hurt you.

322
00:33:22,774 --> 00:33:24,526
The game is over for you.

323
00:33:26,194 --> 00:33:29,656
No... I have to win this...

324
00:33:29,989 --> 00:33:31,616
To save your mother?

325
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:41,584
Coming from a man
who felt humiliated at her very existence.

326
00:33:43,002 --> 00:33:45,088
Aren't you glad she's out of the picture?

327
00:33:49,717 --> 00:33:52,971
She's too sick to survive much longer.

328
00:33:53,721 --> 00:33:55,348
It would be futile to save her.

329
00:33:58,351 --> 00:34:02,897
Her life is worthless.

330
00:34:06,776 --> 00:34:08,903
What do you know?

331
00:34:12,365 --> 00:34:14,284
She's my mother!

332
00:34:15,785 --> 00:34:20,790
There's so much I need to tell her...
She deserves to be happy!

333
00:34:31,092 --> 00:34:34,721
It's too late...
You should have told her earlier.

334
00:34:55,783 --> 00:34:57,201
Don't do it!

335
00:34:59,829 --> 00:35:01,247
Kuranosuke...

336
00:35:03,833 --> 00:35:06,252
you always made me so happy.

337
00:35:36,199 --> 00:35:37,492
Mother...

338
00:35:40,370 --> 00:35:43,748
Mother... Mother...

339
00:35:51,172 --> 00:35:52,382
Mother...

340
00:36:27,083 --> 00:36:29,502
CHECKPOINT 4 CLEARED.

341
00:36:32,213 --> 00:36:33,631
Oh, thank God.

342
00:36:38,302 --> 00:36:40,722
I made it...

343
00:36:53,151 --> 00:36:57,780
ANOTHER DISQUALIFIED.
FOUR REMAIN.

344
00:37:06,789 --> 00:37:11,085
ANOTHER DISQUALIFIED.
FOUR REMAIN.

345
00:37:36,778 --> 00:37:39,947
KURANOSHUKE HIGA HAS BEEN DISQUALIFIED.

346
00:37:56,172 --> 00:38:01,052
Good morning, Mother...

347
00:38:03,471 --> 00:38:07,266
The kachu-yu was delicious.

348
00:38:08,810 --> 00:38:10,228
Thank you, Mother.

349
00:38:14,023 --> 00:38:17,193
Kuranosuke! I made kachu-yu!

350
00:38:17,318 --> 00:38:20,655
Yes! I'll help out too.

351
00:38:29,831 --> 00:38:31,833
Have a good day at work.

352
00:38:33,835 --> 00:38:35,211
Take care.

353
00:38:39,966 --> 00:38:43,678
Thank you for buying me that mitt.

354
00:38:58,484 --> 00:39:00,736
You loved me so much...

355
00:39:03,447 --> 00:39:05,241
I'm sorry...

356
00:39:08,035 --> 00:39:13,833
I couldn't say or do
the things I should have.

357
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:24,260
I'm sorry I couldn't make you happy.

358
00:39:27,430 --> 00:39:33,936
I'm sorry, Mother... I'm sorry...

359
00:39:37,356 --> 00:39:39,400
I'm sorry...

360
00:40:30,284 --> 00:40:31,827
Right here.

361
00:40:34,121 --> 00:40:35,748
It's okay. Thank you.

362
00:40:55,351 --> 00:40:58,062
SHINJUKU CENTRAL POLICE STATION

363
00:41:10,533 --> 00:41:11,701
Another one dead.

364
00:41:13,661 --> 00:41:16,163
A woman was found dead in Naha.

365
00:41:18,457 --> 00:41:21,961
Your gang committed yet another murder.

366
00:41:23,546 --> 00:41:25,464
Inspector, what's the time?

367
00:41:26,841 --> 00:41:28,676
Why do you care?

368
00:42:28,778 --> 00:42:30,154
Sorry.

369
00:42:35,451 --> 00:42:37,161
Japanese...?

370
00:42:47,630 --> 00:42:51,258
Please disperse!
It's not safe here, move along!
